<!--
  ===================================================================
  Online Library — XML data design
  ===================================================================
  Source of truth for the structure: /data/library_schema.sql
  Source of truth for the values:    /data/library_data.sql

  Mapping from the relational (4NF) model to this XML tree:
    - isbn                     -> attribute "isbn" on <book>
                                   (isbn is the natural business key /
                                   UNIQUE column on table "libros")
    - titulo                   -> <title>
    - anio_publicacion         -> <publicationYear>
    - precio                   -> <price currency="MXN">
    - stock                    -> <stock>
    - id_formato -> formatos   -> <format>  (1:N libro -> formato)
    - libro_autor (N:M)        -> <authors><author>...</author></authors>
    - libro_genero (N:M)       -> <genres><genre>...</genre></genres>
    - imagenes_libro (1:N)     -> <images><image cover="true|false">...
    - libro_concepto (N:M with -> <concepts><concept name="...">
      its own "definicion")         <definition>...</definition></concept>

  Multivalued, independent attributes (author, genre, image — see the
  MVD analysis at the top of library_schema.sql) are each modeled as
  their own repeatable child collection, mirroring the bridge tables
  libro_autor / libro_genero / imagenes_libro. The book-concept pair
  keeps its own "definition" text, mirroring table libro_concepto,
  where the same concept can be defined differently per book.
  ===================================================================
-->
